FUNCTION base clamp
INPUTS: number (number): the value to keep inside the limits
        lower (number or nothing): the smallest allowed value, or nothing if there is no smallest
        upper (number or nothing): the biggest allowed value, or nothing if there is no biggest
OUTPUT: number: the input value, or the nearest limit if it was outside the limits
SIDE EFFECTS: NONE
FAILS WHEN: never. It stops with no error for any input.

1. IF number is not equal to itself (this only happens for "not a number")
     RETURN number unchanged
2. IF upper is given
     2.1 IF number is bigger than upper
           set number to upper
3. IF lower is given
     3.1 IF number is smaller than lower
           set number to lower
4. RETURN number